          "id": "tw4-e8",
          "type": "WORD_ORDER",
          "translation": "The train station isn't far.",
          "answer": "Der Bahnhof ist nicht weit.",
          "distractors": ["kein", "nah"]
        },
        {
          "id": "tw4-e9",
          "type": "TEACH",
          "title": "kein or nicht?",
          "body": "Both make a sentence negative, but they're used differently:\n\n- **kein** goes before a noun that would otherwise have *ein*, or no article at all.\n- **nicht** is for everything else: verbs, words like *weit*, and nouns with *der, die, das*.",
          "examples": [
            { "text": "Das ist kein Hotel.", "translation": "That's not a hotel.", "hint": "ein Hotel → kein Hotel" },
